\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Carrier (green) and sideband (blue) field amplitudes $J_\ell (\beta )$ vs.\ sideband order $\ell $, at the four \textit  {ExampleModulationRegimes} values. Under-modulated ($\beta =0.3$): almost all the field stays in the carrier. Optimal ($\beta \approx 1.08$, this project's running example): the carrier/sideband amplitude product $J_0(\beta )J_1(\beta )$ is maximized. Over-modulated ($\beta =1.7$): field has moved past the optimum into higher-order sidebands, and the product has fallen again. Carrier null ($\beta =2.4048$, the first zero of $J_0$): the carrier line vanishes entirely.}}{16}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sideband-regimes}{{7}{16}{Carrier (green) and sideband (blue) field amplitudes $J_\ell (\beta )$ vs.\ sideband order $\ell $, at the four \textit {ExampleModulationRegimes} values. Under-modulated ($\beta =0.3$): almost all the field stays in the carrier. Optimal ($\beta \approx 1.08$, this project's running example): the carrier/sideband amplitude product $J_0(\beta )J_1(\beta )$ is maximized. Over-modulated ($\beta =1.7$): field has moved past the optimum into higher-order sidebands, and the product has fallen again. Carrier null ($\beta =2.4048$, the first zero of $J_0$): the carrier line vanishes entirely}{figure.7}{}}
